# Run the test suite before every push. The frontend CI (.github/workflows/
# ci.yml) gates on `npm test`, but there was no local gate — so a commit that
# broke the SuperAdminDashboard tests was pushed and only caught by a red CI
# run (2026-07-23). This blocks that push locally, matching the backend repo.
#
# Lint first, and blocking since 2026-10-05, when it reached zero problems.
# It ran in CI as informational for months while the count grew to 53, and
# several of those were real bugs (a docs search that searched nothing, an
# error the signup wizard computed and never showed). It is cheap and runs
# before the slower tests so a lint failure is reported in seconds.
npm run lint && npm test
